{"kind":"report","text":"Checker review of H1, the local celld project and public service origin, at exact head 7285dee5f69708133774572b61be64136ddec2bf (tree c88a5a4b9a15d029e15872ac77e188e472691822), for request 99918e60 as amended by 8a50aa07, under builder promise e45fcdef. Verdict: APPROVED.\n\nI read the implementation note 56bb5aec first, then the request, the amendment and section 4.1 of the self-hosting note. Then I read every production and configuration change from Main 248edb41, the CI workflow, the smoke and proxy scripts, and the new tests.\n\n## What I checked\n\n- Base and delta. The head descends from Main 248edb41 through 8 commits. They change exactly the 34 paths named by the 34 artifacts, one artifact per path. None of the artifacts has been superseded. The worktree was clean at the head.\n- Evidence:\n  - The committed manifest has SHA-256 91c45c48…, as stated.\n  - All 169 entries match their recorded size and hash. No entry in the folder is writable.\n  - The root SHA256SUMS has SHA-256 3eb2b218…, and all its 168 lines are OK.\n  - The report tail's SHA256SUMS has SHA-256 a0d3e08b…, and all its 15 lines are OK.\n  - The follow-up patch has SHA-256 eb64d346…, as stated.\n  - The checkpoint trees match the note: ef2f4bea is 14aee9aa, 27be0284 is d0f356a6 and 7985f0fc is 4c74a622. In each receipt the source before and after the run is identical.\n- Gate. The one gate at ef2f4bea exited 1. Native has 821 passed, 1 failed and 2 skipped. Node, Counting and plain passed, and every gate step has a recorded time. The single failure is the new host-none health case: create answered `refused` instead of `accepted`.\n- Proxy run at 7985f0fc. The run exited 0. Its result records:\n  - configured create 201;\n  - unset, forwarded-only and wrong-service creates 403;\n  - a different Host accepted;\n  - two MCP sessions initialized, with two room tool calls;\n  - rotation 200 and retirement 200;\n  - 7 journals verified;\n  - health 200 with sessions `ok` and register `ready`;\n  - both celld processes exited 0 with no signal.\n- Documents:\n  - check-doc-links on an export of the head: 723 links, 0 broken.\n  - check-notes 248edb41..7285dee5: 0 warnings.\n  - check-commit-messages: 8 checked, 0 flagged.\n  - `git diff --check`: clean.\n  - The note is 19,122 bytes.\n\nI reran no suite and no proxy.\n\n## The follow-up after the failed gate\n\nThe gate did not pass, and this review does not call it a pass. I assessed the follow-up under \"Follow-up after a gate\" in docs/testing.md. It meets each condition:\n- The gate failed in one test file only.\n- From ef2f4bea to 27be0284, only packages/scope/test/health.test.ts and the note change. From 27be0284 to the head, only the note and its manifest change.\n- No other file imports health.test.ts.\n- The repair adds `timeOf` to an existing import. It changes the install intent's `notAfter` from `at(60)` to `timeOf(life.now() + 60_000)`. That value is fixture input, not a test timeout, and the 60-second duration is the same. No case, assertion or test timeout changed.\n- At 27be0284 the Scope compiler exited 0, and the whole owning file passed: 5 cases, 0 failed, 0 skipped.\n- The gate reached every stage, so no stage needed a continuation.\n\nThe documented exception therefore applies. The gate and the follow-up remain separate results.\n\n## Architecture\n\nThe change is narrow and matches the request and the amendment.\n\n`readPublicOrigin` is the one reader of `PUBLIC_ORIGIN`:\n- An unset value keeps the request URL origin, as before.\n- A supplied value must already be an exact canonical origin of at most 2048 printable ASCII bytes. It must use HTTPS, or HTTP on a loopback address.\n- Anything else gives null, and each caller then refuses: 404 on the demo offer, 503 on the application routes and MCP.\n\nThe test covers case, default port, path, query, fragment, user information, `localhost`, whitespace and length.\n\nThe callers are the ones the amendment names:\n- hosted MCP creation (the registry's `service`);\n- the applications route's deployment default and screen context;\n- the page redirect's host selection;\n- the sandbox entrypoint;\n- the demo offer's origin checks.\n\nHosted MCP code is unchanged. The Worker passes the public origin to `registry.create`, and `bound` and the link check compare against it. The agent's `control` already used its stored `row.config.service`, so dropping its unused fourth argument changes nothing. An explicit `DEPLOYMENT` still takes precedence over the application default.\n\nThe sandbox gateway first binds the public origin to the trusted descriptor. It then runs the existing path and method matcher on the unchanged transport URL. With `PUBLIC_ORIGIN` unset, the descriptor is passed through unchanged.\n\nThe celld project re-exports the production room entry with a two-line shim. It keeps the four object bindings and the three migration tags of apps/room/wrangler.jsonc. The request named three bindings and two migrations, but Main added ScopeIndex since then, so matching the production file is correct. The project omits the Cloudflare-only keys.\n\nThe page and MCP routes already call the scope API in process, so the `api(env.SCOPES)` condition was met before this head. `ScopeService` stays, for R14 1/2.\n\nThe smoke script takes PHASE=plan or PHASE=run, with BASE and DAP_HOME. The CI job runs the kept proxy driver against `celld dev` for changes under packages/scope, packages/mcp and apps/room. No native definition, wire form, kernel bound or historical pin changes.\n\n## Security\n\n- No forwarded header supplies identity. The witness signs creates for the public origin and sends `Forwarded`, `X-Forwarded-Host` and `X-Forwarded-Proto` with `PUBLIC_ORIGIN` unset. That create is refused with 403 `service`. A different Host does not override the setting, and a wrong signed service is refused, for creation and for rotation.\n- An invalid setting fails closed before any protected object is selected. On `/mcp` the check comes after the bearer form check and before the agent lookup.\n- Authority, signature, body, deadline, membership, rotation and retirement checks are unchanged.\n- The CI job has `contents: read` and no secrets. It verifies the release attestation before it decompresses the binary. The proxy driver checks that the binary's version is the pin and records its hash.\n- The celld project contains no secret. `.dev.vars` and `.celld/` are ignored, and the smoke never prints invitations, signatures or keys.\n\nTwo points, not blocking:\n\n1. The celld project's wrangler.json uses the Worker name `artroom-scope`, which is the name of the production register Worker. Running `wrangler deploy` in apps/room/celld would replace that Worker's code, bindings and plain variables with the local configuration. For example, DEPLOYMENT would become `dap-celld-local` and the Artifacts binding would be removed. The classes and migration tags are the same, so `npm run deploy:scope` would undo it. Nothing in this head runs Wrangler in that directory, and docs/celld.md uses only `celld dev`. A distinct name would remove this risk. It would also remove most of the new `entryIdentity` logic in scripts/security-settings.mjs, but it would add a deployment column to the settings rows. I leave this for the planner to decide, for example in H3 or in R14 2/2, which already edits these configurations.\n2. The workflow pins `actions/checkout@v6` and `actions/setup-node@v6` by major tag, not by commit. With read-only permission and no secrets, this is acceptable. This is the repository's first workflow, so the planner may want to set a rule now.\n\n## Simplification\n\nProduction source is small: public-origin.ts has 18 lines, and the edits to worker.ts, route.ts, bindings.ts and demo-creation.ts are about 50 lines. Most of the added lines are the proxy driver (358), the smoke (186), the manifest and the settings-inventory shim logic. Two points, not blocking:\n\n1. The request asks for the celld version \"pinned in one file\". apps/room/celld/celld.version holds it, but scripts/test-celld-proxy.mjs also requires the literal `v0.6.2`, at lines 63 and 91. A version bump must edit both files. It would fail loudly rather than silently. The driver could compare the binary against the file's value only.\n2. The workflow's path filter omits packages/cli, packages/platform, packages/derive and packages/bytes, although the smoke runs the CLI and those packages. The request named three paths, and the note states this limit, so the condition is met.\n\n## Conclusions\n\n- Architecture: approved.\n- Security: approved. Identity comes only from configuration or the request URL, never from forwarded headers. Invalid configuration fails closed before any object is selected. The authority checks are unchanged. The shared Worker name is left to the planner.\n- Simplification: approved, with the second version literal and the path filter noted.\n- Gate: the failed gate at ef2f4bea remains failed. The isolated follow-up at 27be0284 meets the docs/testing.md conditions.\n\nThis approval covers the software head only. A remote CI run, any deployed proxy, and the H3 kit are not covered. The landing check will follow the landing.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:56bb5aec33b061af9edc8959a8424733d5851789","binding":"assigned","head":"7285dee5f69708133774572b61be64136ddec2bf","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:25a63071b4d761160d4e80a07c993f84de329b0a\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:e45fcdefbfa331bb4527fda5372e0b22fb758c82\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:ed37a6c92b0049d4c7028f62cb7dcf19f8c53a91","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"approved"}}